# Governance Proposal: Update nasa-archive path in risk_classifier.py

**Proposer:** Ganesha (Claude Code CLI)
**Date:** 2026-02-25T00:00:00Z
**Type:** Configuration Change
**Trust Level:** ENGINEER (3)

## Summary
Repo `nasa-archive` was renamed to `safe-app-nasa-archive` on GitHub as part of the SAFE app rebranding (all SAFE apps now use `safe-app-*` prefix). The T3 pattern in risk_classifier.py must reflect the new folder name so the risk tier continues to apply correctly.

## Proposed Changes
**File:** core/risk_classifier.py
**Location:** T3_PATTERNS list, line 44

### File: core/risk_classifier.py

Change from:
    r"[/\\]nasa-archive",

Change to:
    r"[/\\]safe-app-nasa-archive",

## Rationale
- Local folder renamed from `nasa-archive` to `safe-app-nasa-archive` to match GitHub rename
- Without this update, writes to the nasa-archive repo would fall through to T3 via the generic GitHub catch-all, but explicit pattern is correct practice
- No behavioral change — same T3 tier, same effect

## Risk Assessment
- **Risk Level:** MINIMAL
- **Reversible:** YES — revert the string
- **Dependencies:** Local folder `nasa-archive` must have been renamed to `safe-app-nasa-archive` first (done)
- **Testing:** `python Willow/core/risk_classifier.py "C:\Users\Sean\Documents\GitHub\safe-app-nasa-archive\data\test.json"` should return T3

## ΔE Impact
Expected ΔE: +0.001 (path string update only)

## Implementation
```diff
--- a/core/risk_classifier.py
+++ b/core/risk_classifier.py
@@ -41,7 +41,7 @@
 T3_PATTERNS = [
     r"[/\\]safe-app-",
     r"[/\\]scoot-",
-    r"[/\\]nasa-archive",
+    r"[/\\]safe-app-nasa-archive",
     r"[/\\]die-namic-website",
```

